Tests for riscos-mupen64plus
============================

gl16 opens an SDL window with an OpenGL context, as the emulator's Rice video plugin does, and
draws a textured quad: 32-pixel red and white squares, 8 across, with the red going to magenta
from left to right, on a blue background. It runs for 3000 frames, then quits.

Run it by double-clicking RunGL16. Its report (the desktop's pixel format, the GL renderer, and
any heap corruption it found) is written to gl16out here.

In a 16M colour desktop mode it draws correctly. In a 64K colour mode (16 bpp), the window
shows the left half of the picture stretched to the full width, with the wrong colours. See
docs/RISC3D-0.17-report.md in the riscos-mupen64plus repository.

Source: riscos/probe/gl16.c. GPL-2.0, as the rest of the port.
